  "premise_review": [
    "The complete original contract stores an old-provider AdelicSpectralSheaf, the whole Zeros:Type carrier, the exact dependent alignment, and a separate SpectralBoundaryCriticalLineBridge alignment. All fields remain; no nonempty carrier or bridge construction is inferred.",
    "The complete AllZerosOnCriticalLine predicate quantifies over C.Zeros and uses the exact C.alignment.zeroData. Its theorem retains C and the full intro-z/exact critical_line_from_spectral_boundary_alignment C.alignment C.criticalLineBridge z proof.",
    "Full original alignment context explicitly requires its separate B.forcesCriticalLine on A.alignmentHolds; the aligned Prop alone supplies no critical-line forcing. Its theorem named does_not_force_critical_line_alone actually proves True, not a nonderivability result. The new wrapper claims only the exact conditional consequence, never RH, a constructed adelic sheaf, analytic L-function zeros or new theorem priority.",
    "Full LFunctionZero/CriticalLine context was read. Root-captured ZeroTypology and DualPivot names do not bind their unmatched original Core/ module paths. Every historical provider/import stays unchanged and unreplayed; context or prior derived modules are not substituted."
  ],
